2026-08-29 01:37:48 [DEBUG] llm.engine: ARGS: ('\n        You are a workflow assistant. Extract parameters for the intent "select_idea_by_reference".\n\n        User message:\n        select this: 19-1392 Argued: 12/01/21 Case Description: The case centers on a Mississippi law prohibiting abortions\n\n        Parameter schema for this intent:\n        - "reference": type=string, required=True\n\n        Extraction instructions for this intent:\n        - The "reference" parameter must always be set to the idea\'s "id" field.\n- Never return the idea name or description.\n- Use the relevant context block (which lists ideas with id, name, and description)\n  to determine which idea the user is referring to.\n- If the user refers to an idea by name, description, or position (e.g., "the immigration case",\n  "idea 3", "the fed reserve governor case"), resolve it to the correct idea and return its id.\n\n\n\nRelevant context:\nideas:\n  - id: 25-197, name: T. M. v. Univ. of MD Medical Sys. Corp., description: The Supreme Court is being asked to clarify the scope of a legal doctrine known as Rooker-Feldman, which limits the jurisdiction of lower courts to challenge final decisions from state high courts.\n  - id: 20-322, name: Garland, Att\'y Gen. v. Gonzalez, description: The Supreme Court is deciding whether a lower court can issue a class-wide injunction to stop certain immigration provisions, and if so, under what circumstances.\n  - id: 23-726, name: Moyle v. United States, description: The case Moyle v. United States concerns a dispute over the scope of the Emergency Medical Treatment and Active Labor Act (EMTALA), with Petitioners arguing that it does not require doctors to perform medical treatments that violate state law, particularly in the context of abortion.\n  - id: 19-1392, name: Dobbs v. Jackson Women\'s Health, description: The case centers on a Mississippi law prohibiting abortions after 15 weeks, with exceptions for women\'s health and life. The lower courts struck down the law, citing Roe v. Wade and Casey as requiring protection of unborn life only after viability. The issue is whether the Constitution should be interpreted to allow states to regulate abortion before viability.\n  - id: 19-508, name: AMG Capital Management, LLC v. FTC, description: The Supreme Court is deciding whether the Federal Trade Commission can seek a permanent injunction under Section 13(b) of the FTC Act, or if it must use a different provision to obtain monetary relief for past consumer harm.\n  - id: 23-1275, name: Medina v. Planned Parenthood South Atlantic, description: The case concerns whether Congress has the authority to require South Carolina to allow any qualified provider to participate in a healthcare program, with the state\'s consent.\n  - id: 21-463, name: Whole Woman\'s Health v. Jackson, description: The case Whole Woman\'s Health v. Jackson is about whether a Texas law that severely restricts abortion rights can be enforced in state courts, and if so, whether it violates federal law by allowing individual citizens to sue abortion providers for violating the law.\n  - id: 22-210, name: Dupree v. Younger, description: The Supreme Court is deciding whether a party must reargue a legal issue at trial to preserve it for appeal, or if the issue is automatically preserved after a summary judgment ruling.\n  - id: 20-1263, name: Gallardo v. Marstiller, description: The Gallardo v. Marstiller case is about whether Medicaid benefits are a loan to be repaid or a true benefit, with the state seeking reimbursement from third-party liabilities for medical expenses.\n  - id: 21-806, name: Health and Hospital Corp. v. Talevski, description: The case, Health and Hospital Corp. v. Talevski, centers on the obligation of nursing facilities to protect and promote patient rights under a specific statute.\n  - id: 23-477, name: United States v. Skrmetti, description: This case is about a Tennessee law that bans certain medications for minors to treat gender dysphoria, with the state arguing it\'s necessary to protect adolescent health.\n  - id: 20-219, name: Cummings v. Premier Rehab, description: The case is about whether victims of intentional discrimination can receive emotional distress damages under certain federal laws, with the Supreme Court considering a lower court\'s decision that such damages are not available.\n  - id: 23-1038, name: FDA v. Wages and White Lion, description: The Supreme Court is considering whether the FDA was correct to deny authorization for flavored e-cigarettes, citing concerns that they attract youth to tobacco use.\n  - id: 20-1641, name: Marietta Memorial Hosp. v. Davita Inc., description: The case concerns a dispute over the Medicare Secondary Payer Act, which coordinates benefits between group health plans and Medicare for individuals with end-stage renal disease. The issue is whether a group health plan must provide the same benefits to all participants, including those with end-stage renal disease, during a 30-month coordination period. The case is Marietta Memorial Hosp. v. Davita Inc.\n\nFollow these rules:\n- Extract parameters strictly according to the schema.\n- Apply the extraction instructions above.\n- Use context only when the user refers indirectly (e.g., "it", "that one").\n- If a parameter cannot be extracted, set it to null.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON. No commentary.\n\nReturn JSON in this format:\n{\n    "parameters": {\n        <param_name>: <value or null>\n    },\n    "reasoning": "<brief explanation>"\n}\n',)
